xt` (event text embeddings)\n\n3. **Fusion & Alignment** (Module 3)\n   - Cross-attention mechanism for multimodal fusion\n   - Aligns spatial-temporal and text embeddings\n   - Outputs: `H_fused` (fused embeddings)\n\n4. **Decoder** (Module 4)\n   - Fully connected layer for final prediction\n   - Outputs: Traffic forecasts (`Y_hat`)\n\n### 2.2 Key Architectural Features\n\n**Multi-Modal Fusion Strategy**:\n- Two modalities: Structured (traffic time series) + Unstructured (event text)\n- Cross-attention mechanism enables deep interaction between modalities\n- Superior to simple concatenation or gating approaches\n\n**Event-Aware Processing**:\n- Dynamic event extraction based on spatio-temporal context\n- Considers events occurring 60-115 minutes after each timestamp\n- Event types: LA news, severe weather, concerts, crime\n\n**Graph Neural Network Base**:\n- D2STGNN with 5 decoupled spatial-temporal layers\n- Dual-resolution spatial modeling\n- Captures both periodic and non-periodic traffic patterns\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Files and Locations\n\n### 3.1 Event Processing Module\n\n**File**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/FUSE-Traffic/gemini.py`\n\n**Purpose**: Demonstrates event data processing pipeline using Google Cloud APIs\n\n**Key Functions**:\n```python\ndef read_time_from_file(file_path)\n  - Reads temporal data from HDF5 traffic files\n  - Returns timestamps as datetime64 arrays\n\ndef read_coordinates_from_file(file_path)\n  - Parses sensor location CSV files\n  - Format: index, sensor_id, latitude, longitude\n  - Returns formatted coordinate strings\n\ndef main()\n  - Main event processing pipeline\n  - Uses Gemini 2.5 Pro to identify events\n  - Generates text embeddings via Vertex AI\n  - Saves embeddings to compressed numpy format (.npz)\n```\n\n**Data Flow**:\n1. Read sensor coordinates and timestamps\n2. Generate prompts with location/time context\n3. Query Gemini 2.5 Pro for events\n4. Generate event embeddings (768-dimensional)\n5. Save as METR.npz (float32)\n\n### 3.2 Baseline Configurations\n\n**Files**: `/home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/repos/FUSE-Traffic/baselines/D2STGNN/`\n- `METR-LA.py` (207 sensors, 34,272 timesteps)\n- `PEMS-BAY.py` (325 sensors, 52,116 timesteps)\n- `PEMS03.py` (358 sensors, 26,208 timesteps)\n\n**Configuration Structure** (all three files):\n```python\n# Model Architecture\nMODEL_ARCH = D2STGNN\nMODEL_PARAM = {\n    "num_feat": 1,                      # Single feature (speed/flow)\n    "num_hidden": 32,                   # Hidden dimension\n    "dropout": 0.1,                     # Dropout rate\n    "seq_length": 12,                   # Input sequence length\n    "k_t": 3, "k_s": 2, "gap": 3,      # Temporal/spatial kernels\n    "num_nodes": <dataset_specific>,    # 207/325/358 sensors\n    "adjs": [adjacency matrices],       # Double-transition adjacency\n    "num_layers": 5,                    # Graph layers\n    "num_modalities": 2,                # Dual modality (ST + event)\n    "node_hidden": <10-12>,             # Node embedding dimension\n    "time_emb_dim": <10-12>,            # Temporal embedding dimension\n    "time_in_day_size": 288,            # 5-minute intervals (24h)\n    "day_in_week_size": 7               # Weekly periodicity\n}\n\n# Training Configuration\nCFG.TRAIN = {\n    "NUM_EPOCHS": 100,\n    "OPTIM": "Adam" (lr=0.002, weight_decay=1e-5),\n    "LR_SCHEDULER": "MultiStepLR" (milestones: [1,30,38,46,54,62,70,80]),\n    "LOSS": "masked_mae",\n    "BATCH_SIZE": 64-128 (dataset-dependent),\n    "CLIP_GRAD_PARAM": {"max_norm": 5.0}\n}\n\n# Curriculum Learning\nCFG.TRAIN.CL = {\n    "WARM_EPOCHS": 0 or 30,\n    "CL_EPOCHS": 3-6,\n    "PREDICTION_LENGTH": 12\n}\n\n# Metrics\nMETRICS = ["MAE", "MAPE", "RMSE"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Data Format Requirements\n\n### 4.1 Traffic Data\n- **Format**: HDF5 (.h5 files)\n- **Structure**: N×T tensor (N sensors, T timesteps)\n- **Temporal Resolution**: 5-minute intervals\n- **Preprocessing**: Z-score normalization per channel\n- **Datasets**: METR-LA, PEMS-BAY, PEMS03\n\n### 4.2 Graph Data\n- **Format**: Pickle (.pkl files)\n- **Content**: Adjacency matrices (double-transition)\n- **Type**: Weighted adjacency matrices capturing spatial dependencies\n- **Usage**: Converted to PyTorch tensors during training\n\n### 4.3 Event Data\n- **Source**: Google Gemini API (dynamic queries)\n- **Input**: Sensor coordinates (lat/lon), timestamps\n- **Output**: Text descriptions of events\n- **Embedding**: 768-dimensional vectors via Vertex AI\n- **Storage**: Compressed numpy format (.npz, float32)\n\n### 4.4 Sensor Locations\n- **Format**: CSV (graph_sensor_locations.txt)\n- **Structure**: index, sensor_id, latitude, longitude\n- **Purpose**: Geographic context for event queries\n\n---\n\n## 5. Dependencies and Requirements\n\n### 5.1 Core ML Framework\n- **PyTorch**: Main deep learning framework (via basicts library)\n- **Python Version**: Not explicitly specified (likely 3.7+)\n- **GPU Support**: NVIDIA A6000 tested (48GB VRAM)\n\n### 5.2 Library Dependencies\n\n**basicts Library** (Custom traffic forecasting framework):\n```python\nfrom basicts.metrics import masked_mae, masked_mape, masked_rmse\nfrom basicts.data import TimeSeriesForecastingDataset\nfrom basicts.runners import SimpleTimeSeriesForecastingRunner\nfrom basicts.scaler import ZScoreScaler\nfrom basicts.utils import get_regular_settings, load_adj\n```\n\n**Data Processing**:\n- `pandas`: Data manipulation and HDF5 reading\n- `numpy`: Numerical operations and array handling\n- `h5py`: HDF5 file I/O (implicit via pandas)\n\n**Configuration Management**:\n- `easydict`: Dictionary-style config access\n\n**Progress Tracking**:\n- `tqdm`: Progress bars for event processing\n\n**Visualization/Analysis**:\n- `sklearn.manifold.TSNE`: t-SNE embedding visualization\n- `matplotlib`: Plotting (implicit in analysis)\n\n### 5.3 Google Cloud AI Services\n\n**Required APIs**:\n- **Google Generative AI SDK** (`google.genai`)\n  - Gemini 2.5 Pro API for event retrieval\n  \n- **Vertex AI** (`vertexai.language_models`)\n  - TextEmbeddingModel (text-embedding-005)\n  - 768-dimensional embeddings\n\n**Requirements**:\n- GCP Project ID\n- Service account credentials (JSON)\n- API quotas and billing enabled\n- Supported region (e.g., us-central1)\n\n### 5.4 Installation Pattern\n\n```bash\n# Core dependencies (from baselines)\npip install torch pandas numpy easydict tqdm\n\n# Google Cloud AI\npip install google-genai vertexai\n\n# Optional (for evaluation/visualization)\npip install scikit-learn matplotlib tensorboard\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Model Architecture Details\n\n### 6.1 Spatial-Temporal Graph Encoder\n\n**Base Model**: D2STGNN\n\n**Architecture**:\n- 5 Decoupled Spatial-Temporal Layers\n- Separate spatial and temporal modeling\n- Dynamic correlation learning\n- Output: Spatial-temporal embeddings (`E_st`)\n\n**Hyperparameters**:\n- Hidden dimension: 32\n- Dropout: 0.1\n- Kernel sizes: k_t=3, k_s=2, gap=3\n\n### 6.2 Event Retrieval Process\n\n**LLM Prompting Strategy**:\n\n```\nYou are a traffic analysis assistant for [CITY].\nYou need to consider events occurring Hin to (Hout+Hin-1) minutes \nafter each timestamp that could affect traffic speed.\n\n### Date and Time: [TIMESTAMP]\n### Geographic Coordinates: [COORDINATE_LIST]\n\nFor each sensor, identify nearby events that could impact traffic \n(e.g., LA news, Severe Weather, concerts, crime).\n```\n\n**Output Format**: JSON with event descriptions\n**Event Types Considered**: News, weather, crime, concerts/exhibitions\n**Future Window**: 60-115 minutes ahead (configurable)\n\n### 6.3 Fusion & Alignment Mechanism\n\n**Cross-Attention Layers**:\n```\nMulti-Head Attention (MHA):\n  Query (Q):  E_st (spatial-temporal embeddings)\n  Key (K):    E_text (event embeddings)\n  Value (V):  E_text\n\nAttention(Q, K, V) = softmax(QK^T/√d_k)V\n\nOutput: H_C = LN(MHA(Q,K,V) + E_st)\nFinal: H_fused = LN(H_C + FFN(H_C))\n```\n\n**Components**:\n- Multi-head attention (8 heads typical)\n- Layer normalization between blocks\n- Feed-forward network (MLP)\n- Residual connections\n\n**Embedding Dimension**: 1024 (unified for both modalities)\n\n### 6.4 Decoder\n\n**Simple Design**:\n```python\nYhat = FC(H_fused)\n```\n- Fully connected layer\n- Maps fused embeddings to traffic predictions\n- Maintains temporal structure (N×H_out)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Training Pipeline\n\n### 7.1 Data Splits\n\n**METR-LA & PEMS-BAY**:\n- Training: 70%\n- Validation: 10%\n- Testing: 20%\n\n**PEMS03**:\n- Training: 60%\n- Validation: 20%\n- Testing: 20%\n\n### 7.2 Loss Function\n\n- **Primary Loss**: Masked MAE (Mean Absolute Error)\n- **Masking Strategy**: Handles missing/invalid data points\n\n### 7.3 Optimization\n\n**Optimizer**: Adam\n- Learning rate: 0.002\n- Weight decay: 1e-5\n- Epsilon: 1e-8\n\n**Learning Rate Scheduler**: MultiStepLR\n- Milestones: [1, 30, 38, 46, 54, 62, 70, 80]\n- Gamma (decay factor): 0.5\n\n**Regularization**:\n- Gradient clipping: max_norm=5.0\n- Early stopping: patience=10 epochs\n\n### 7.4 Curriculum Learning (Dataset-Specific)\n\n**METR-LA**:\n- Warm epochs: 0\n- CL epochs: 6\n- Gradually increase prediction length to 12\n\n**PEMS-BAY**:\n- Warm epochs: 30\n- CL epochs: 3\n- Ramp up before curriculum stage\n\n**PEMS03**:\n- Standard curriculum applied\n\n---\n\n## 8. Evaluation and Performance\n\n### 8.1 Evaluation Metrics\n\n```python\nMAE = (1/NT) * Σ|y_hat - y|\nRMSE = √((1/NT) * Σ(y_hat - y)²)\nMAPE = (1/NT) * Σ|y_hat - y|/|y| * 100%\n```\n\n### 8.2 Prediction Horizons\n\n- **Short-term**: 3 steps (15 minutes)\n- **Medium-term**: 6 steps (30 minutes)\n- **Long-term**: 12 steps (60 minutes)\n\n### 8.3 Performance Results (METR-LA)\n\n| Horizon | Method | MAE | RMSE | MAPE(%) |\n|---------|--------|-----|------|---------|\n| 15 min  | FUSE-Traffic | 2.53 | 4.93 | 6.54 |\n| 30 min  | FUSE-Traffic | 2.90 | 5.89 | 8.02 |\n| 60 min  | FUSE-Traffic | 3.39 | 7.28 | 9.84 |\n\n**Baseline Comparison**: FUSE-Traffic outperforms:\n- GraphWaveNet, STWave, D2STGNN (GNN-only)\n- DIGC-Net (manually engineered events)\n- STORM, T3 (text-based events, static)\n- UrbanGPT, STD-PLM (LLM-based)\n\n### 8.4 Robustness on Event Impact Types\n\n**Event Impact Categories**:\n- No Impact: ~60% of timestamps\n- Minor Impact: ~10-15%\n- Moderate Impact: ~15%\n- High Impact: ~5-10%\n\n**Key Finding**: FUSE-Traffic shows most improvement under high-impact event conditions.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Ablation Studies\n\n### 9.1 Prompt Design Impact\n\n**Five Variants Tested**:\n1. **P1 (Full Feature)**: All event types (news, weather, concerts, crime)\n2. **P2 (Single Event)**: Most influential event only\n3. **P3 (w/o weather)**: News, concerts, crime only\n4. **P4 (w/o crime)**: News, weather, concerts only\n5. **P5 (Zero Shot)**: No examples provided\n\n**Findings**:\n- Weather events: Critical for PEMS03 (storms affect traffic significantly)\n- Crime events: Important for METR-LA (downtown LA has high crime frequency)\n- Examples in prompts: Improves LLM reasoning\n\n### 9.2 Fusion Mechanism Design\n\n**Compared Variants**:\n- **Cross-Attention**: Best performance\n- **Gating Mechanism**: Moderate degradation\n- **Simple Addition**: Minor degradation\n- **Concatenation**: Worst performance\n\n**Conclusion**: Cross-attention effectively aligns multimodal representations.\n\n### 9.3 Hyperparameter Sensitivity\n\n**MLP Layers**: Optimal at 2 layers\n**Text Embedding Dimension**: Optimal at 512\n**Performance Curve**: Improves then plateaus with model expansion\n\n---\n\n## 10. Integration with LibCity\n\n### 10.1 Model Integration Considerations\n\n1. **Architecture Adaptation**:\n   - Integrate D2STGNN as base model\n   - Maintain dual-modality fusion\n   - Preserve multi-graph handling\n   - Implement cross-attention fusion block\n\n2. **Event Data Pipeline**:\n   - Option A: Integrate Google Cloud APIs (requires GCP setup)\n   - Option B: Replace with local LLM (e.g., Ollama, LLaMA)\n   - Option C: Implement local text embedding (sentence-transformers)\n\n3. **Configuration Format**:\n   - Convert EasyDict to LibCity\'s YAML/JSON format\n   - Maintain parameter compatibility across datasets\n   - Support curriculum learning configuration\n\n4. **Data Format Adaptation**:\n   - HDF5 compatibility (may already be in LibCity)\n   - Adjacency matrix loading from pickle files\n   - Event embedding integration\n   - Sensor coordinate handling\n\n### 10.2 Key Files to Reference\n\n- **Model Class Location**: Should reference D2STGNN from basicts\n- **Training Script**: baselines/D2STGNN/METR-LA.py pattern\n- **Config Template**: EasyDict configuration pattern\n- **Data Loading**: TimeSeriesForecastingDataset from basicts\n\n---\n\n## 11. Notable Implementation Details\n\n### 11.1 Text Encoder Freezing\n\n**Strategy**: Freeze pretrained text encoder during training\n- Preserves generalization learned from massive text corpora\n- Reduces trainable parameters\n- Stabilizes training with sparse event data\n\n### 11.2 Event Temporal Alignment\n\n**Event Window**: Future-looking (60-115 minutes)\n- Anticipates event impact on traffic\n- Non-causal knowledge integration\n- Practical for forecasting tasks\n\n### 11.3 Spatial Event Matching\n\n**Coordinate-Based Matching**:\n- Events matched to sensor geographic locations\n- Considers proximity for event relevance\n- Enables location-specific event handling\n\n### 11.4 Curriculum Learning Purpose\n\n**Gradual Complexity Increase**:\n- PEMS-BAY: 30 warm epochs + 3 CL epochs\n- Helps with difficult datasets\n- Prevents premature convergence\n- Improves long-term prediction accuracy\n\n---\n\n## 12. Comparison with Baselines\n\n### 12.1 Architecture Paradigms\n\n| Model | Input Fusion | Intermediate Fusion | Output Fusion | Alignment |\n|-------|--------------|-------------------|---------------|-----------|\n| STORM | No | Yes (Add) | No | Gating |\n| T3 | No | No | Yes | None |\n| UrbanGPT | Yes (Prompt) | No | No | None |\n| FUSE-Traffic | No | Yes (Add) | No | Cross-Attention |\n\n### 12.2 Event Data Handling\n\n- **Manual Features**: Limited generalization\n- **Static Text Data**: Requires curation, incomplete\n- **LLM-only**: Computationally expensive\n- **FUSE-Traffic**: Dynamic LLM queries + efficient GNN fusion\n\n---\n\n## 13. Case Study: Event Impact Demonstration\n\n### 13.1 Scenario\n- **Location**: Sensor 82 (METR-LA)\n- **Time**: March 1-2, 2012, 11:00-18:40\n- **Event**: Traffic accident at Sherman Oaks Castle Park (17:40-18:40)\n\n### 13.2 Results\n\n**Off-Peak Hour (11:00-12:00)**:\n- Ground truth: 63-68 mph with minor fluctuations\n- Model w/o events: Constant 66 mph (misses volatility)\n- Model w/ events: Matches ground truth volatility\n\n**Peak Hour (17:40-18:40)**:\n- Ground truth: Rapid drop from 60+ to 0 mph\n- Model w/o events: Delayed response, significant lag\n- Model w/ events: Captures sharp decline, anticipates impact\n\n**t-SNE Embedding Analysis**:\n- Without fusion: Only 2-3 clusters (underdifferentiated)\n- With fusion: Clear clusters for different impact types\n- Enables fine-grained traffic pattern recognition\n\n---\n\n## 14. External Dependencies and APIs\n\n### 14.1 Google Cloud Services\n\n**Required Setup**:\n1. GCP Project creation\n2. Service account setup\n3. Enable APIs:\n   - Generative AI API (Gemini)\n   - Vertex AI API\n4. Authenticate via service account JSON\n\n**API Quotas**:\n- Gemini API calls: Variable pricing\n- Vertex AI embeddings: Per-request billing\n- Consider preprocessing caching to reduce costs\n\n### 14.2 Cost Considerations\n\n- Event retrieval for all sensors + all timestamps can be expensive\n- Potential optimization: Cache event queries, batch processing\n- Alternative: Use local/open-source models\n\n---\n\n## 15. Summary: Key Takeaways for Migration\n\n### Architecture Strengths\n1. Effective multimodal fusion via cross-attention\n2. Dynamic event querying addresses limitations of static datasets\n3. Superior performance especially on high-impact events\n4. Outperforms both GNN-only and LLM-only baselines\n\n### Technical Innovations\n1. First to combine LLM dynamic querying with GNN traffic modeling\n2. Careful prompt design for event relevance\n3. Frozen text encoder preserves pretrained knowledge\n4. Curriculum learning for difficult datasets\n\n### Integration Challenges\n1. Dependency on Google Cloud APIs (external service)\n2. Requires GCP credentials for full functionality\n3. Event embedding computation can be costly at scale\n4. basicts library dependency\n\n### Recommended Migration Path\n1. Adapt D2STGNN model to LibCity interface\n2. Implement cross-attention fusion module\n3. Replace Google APIs with local LLM alternative\n4. Convert configurations to LibCity YAML/JSON format\n5. Ensure compatibility with LibCity data loaders\n\n---\n\n## 16. References and Resources\n\n**Paper**: FUSE-Traffic: Fusion of Unstructured and Structured Data for Event-aware Traffic Forecasting\n**Conference**: SIGSPATIAL 2025\n**Authors**: Chenyang Yu, Xinpeng Xie, Yan Huang, Chenxi Qiu\n**GitHub**: https://github.com/GeoAICenter/FUSE-Traffic_Sigspatial2025\n**DOI**: 10.1145/3748636.3762776\n\n**Baseline Models Referenced**:\n- D2STGNN (Shao et al., 2022)\n- GraphWaveNet (Wu et al., 2019)\n- STORM (Hong et al., 2024)\n- T3 (Han et al., 2024)\n- UrbanGPT (Li et al., 2024)\n- STD-PLM (Huang et al., 2025)\n\n---\n\n**Document Generated**: January 23, 2026\n**Analysis Scope**: Complete code and paper review for LibCity migration planning\nEOF\ncat /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/FUSE-TRAFFIC_COMPREHENSIVE_ANALYSIS.md\n', 'description': 'Create comprehensive FUSE-Traffic analysis document'}
[ERR] 2026-01-23 02:22:25 | INFO | Tool Bash called with {'command': 'cat > /home/wangwenrui/private/shk/agentCity/FUSE-TRAFFIC_CODE_SNIPPETS.md << \'EOF\'\n# FUSE-Traffic: Key Code Snippets and Implementation Details\n\n## 1. Event Processing with Google Gemini (gemini.py)\n\n### 1.1 Core Imports\n```python\nfrom google import genai\nfrom google.genai.types import HttpOptions\nfrom google.genai import types\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nimport vertexai\nfrom vertexai.language_models import TextEmbeddingModel\nfrom tqdm import tqdm\n```\n\n### 1.2 Event Retrieval Setup\n```python\nPROJECT_ID = "xxxx"                    # GCP Project ID\nMODEL_ID = "text-embedding-005"        # Vertex AI embedding model\nLOCATION = "xxxx"                      # GCP region (e.g., us-central1)\nCOORDINATE_FILE_PATH = "graph_sensor_locations.txt"\ndata_file_path = \'datasets/raw_data/METR-LA/METR-LA.h5\'\n```\n\n### 1.3 Read Temporal Data from HDF5\n```python\ndef read_time_from_file(file_path):\n    df = pd.read_hdf(file_path)\n    return df.index.values.astype(\'datetime64[m]\')\n```\n\n### 1.4 Read Sensor Coordinates\n```python\ndef read_coordinates_from_file(file_path):\n    """\n    Reads coordinate pairs from CSV file (format: index,sensor_id,lat,lon)\n    Returns list of formatted coordinate strings\n    """\n    coordinates = []\n    try:\n        with open(file_path, \'r\') as f:\n            is_header = True\n            for line in f:\n                if is_header:\n                    is_header = False\n                    continue\n                \n                line = line.strip()\n                if line:\n                    try:\n                        parts = line.split(\',\')\n                        if len(parts) >= 4:\n                            lat_str = parts[2].strip()\n                            lon_str = parts[3].strip()\n                            lat = float(lat_str)\n                            lon = float(lon_str)\n                            coordinates.append(f"({lat}° N, {lon}° W)")\n                        else:\n                            print(f"Warning: Skipping malformed line: {line}")\n                    except ValueError:\n                        print(f"Warning: Skipping non-numeric coordinate line: {line}")\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        print(f"ERROR: Coordinate file not found at \'{file_path}\'")\n        return None\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f"ERROR: Failed to read coordinate file: {e}")\n        return None\n    \n    if not coordinates:\n        print(f"ERROR: No valid coordinates found in file")\n        return None\n    \n    return coordinates\n```\n\n### 1.5 LLM-Based Event Extraction\n```python\ndef main():\n    City = \'Los Angeles (LA)\'\n    vertexai.init(project=PROJECT_ID, location=LOCATION)\n    \n    # Read data\n    print(f"\\nReading coordinates from: {COORDINATE_FILE_PATH}")\n    coordinate_list = read_coordinates_from_file(COORDINATE_FILE_PATH)\n    times = read_time_from_file(data_file_path)\n    \n    if coordinate_list is None:\n        sys.exit(1)\n    \n    print(f"Successfully read {len(coordinate_list)} coordinate pairs.")\n    \n    # Initialize Gemini client\n    client = genai.Client(\n        vertexai=True,\n        project=PROJECT_ID,\n        location=LOCATION\n    )\n    \n    text_emds = []\n    \n    # Process each timestamp\n    for i in tqdm(range(0, len(times)), desc="Processing Times"):\n        prompt = f"""\n        You are a traffic analysis assistant for {City}.\n        Below is a list of {len(coordinate_list)} sensor coordinates: {coordinate_list}\n        Here are the timestamps for when the sensors observed activity.\n        You need to consider events occurring 60 to 115 minutes after each timestamp \n        that could affect traffic flow.\n        Timestamps: {times[i]}\n        For each sensor and timestamp, identify nearby event that could impact traffic \n        (e.g., Local news, Severe Weather, concerts, crime).\n        Return a list of {len(coordinate_list)} items for all sensors.\n        """\n        \n        try:\n            response = client.models.generate_content(\n                model="gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25",\n                contents=prompt,\n                config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n                    response_mime_type=\'application/json\',\n                    response_schema={\n                        \'items\': {\n                            \'required\': [\'Event\'],\n                            \'properties\': {\n                                \'Event\': {\n                                    \'type\': \'STRING\',\n                                    \'example\': "Classic Cinema Night at Cinegrill Theater",\n                                    \'description\': "Find nearby event that could influence traffic"\n                                }\n                            },\n                            \'type\': \'Object\'\n                        },\n                        \'type\': \'Array\',\n                    },\n                ),\n            )\n            \n            # Generate embeddings for event text\n            model = TextEmbeddingModel.from_pretrained(MODEL_ID)\n            embeddings = model.get_embeddings([response.text])\n            \n            if embeddings:\n                response_embedding_vector = embeddings[0].values\n                text_emds.append(response_embedding_vector)\n            else:\n                print("Embedding generation returned an empty result.")\n        \n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"\\n--- ERROR during Vertex AI API Call ---")\n            print(f"An error occurred: {e}")\n            print("-------------------------------------\\n")\n    \n    # Save embeddings\n    text_emds = np.array(text_emds, dtype=np.float32)\n    np.savez_compressed(\'METR.npz\', embeddings=text_emds)\n\nif __name__ == "__main__":\n    main()\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Model Configuration Examples\n\n### 2.1 METR-LA Configuration (METR-LA.py)\n\n```python\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport torch\nfrom easydict import EasyDict\nsys.path.append(os.path.abspath(__file__ + \'/../../..\'))\n\nfrom basicts.metrics import masked_mae, masked_mape, masked_rmse\nfrom basicts.data import TimeSeriesForecastingDataset\nfrom basicts.runners import SimpleTimeSeriesForecastingRunner\nfrom basicts.scaler import ZScoreScaler\nfrom basicts.utils import get_regular_settings, load_adj\nfrom .arch import D2STGNN\n\n# Dataset Configuration\nDATA_NAME = \'METR-LA\'\nregular_settings = get_regular_settings(DATA_NAME)\nINPUT_LEN = regular_settings[\'INPUT_LEN\']\nOUTPUT_LEN = regular_settings[\'OUTPUT_LEN\']\nTRAIN_VAL_TEST_RATIO = regular_settings[\'TRAIN_VAL_TEST_RATIO\']\nNORM_EACH_CHANNEL = regular_settings[\'NORM_EACH_CHANNEL\']\nRESCALE = regular_settings[\'RESCALE\']\nNULL_VAL = regular_settings[\'NULL_VAL\']\n\n# Load adjacency matrices\nMODEL_ARCH = D2STGNN\nadj_mx, _ = load_adj("datasets/" + DATA_NAME + "/adj_mx.pkl", "doubletransition")\n\n# Model Parameters\nMODEL_PARAM = {\n    "num_feat": 1,                      # Traffic speed feature\n    "num_hidden": 32,                   # Hidden dimension\n    "dropout": 0.1,                     # Dropout rate\n    "seq_length": 12,                   # Input sequence length (12 * 5min = 60min)\n    "k_t": 3,                           # Temporal kernel size\n    "k_s": 2,                           # Spatial kernel size\n    "gap": 3,                           # Gap parameter\n    "num_nodes": 207,                   # Number of sensors in METR-LA\n    "adjs": [torch.tensor(adj) for adj in adj_mx],  # Adjacency matrices as tensors\n    "num_layers": 5,                    # Number of ST layers\n    "num_modalities": 2,                # Traffic + Events\n    "node_hidden": 10,                  # Node embedding dimension\n    "time_emb_dim": 10,                 # Temporal embedding dimension\n    "time_in_day_size": 288,            # 5-min intervals per day\n    "day_in_week_size": 7,              # Days per week\n}\n\nNUM_EPOCHS = 100\n\n# Main Configuration\nCFG = EasyDict()\nCFG.DESCRIPTION = \'An Example Config\'\nCFG.GPU_NUM = 1\n\n# Runner\nCFG.RUNNER = SimpleTimeSeriesForecastingRunner\n\n# Dataset\nCFG.DATASET = EasyDict()\nCFG.DATASET.NAME = DATA_NAME\nCFG.DATASET.TYPE = TimeSeriesForecastingDataset\nCFG.DATASET.PARAM = EasyDict({\n    \'dataset_name\': DATA_NAME,\n    \'train_val_test_ratio\': TRAIN_VAL_TEST_RATIO,\n    \'input_len\': INPUT_LEN,\n    \'output_len\': OUTPUT_LEN,\n})\n\n# Scaler\nCFG.SCALER = EasyDict()\nCFG.SCALER.TYPE = ZScoreScaler\nCFG.SCALER.PARAM = EasyDict({\n    \'dataset_name\': DATA_NAME,\n    \'train_ratio\': TRAIN_VAL_TEST_RATIO[0],\n    \'norm_each_channel\': NORM_EACH_CHANNEL,\n    \'rescale\': RESCALE,\n})\n\n# Model\nCFG.MODEL = EasyDict()\nCFG.MODEL.NAME = MODEL_ARCH.__name__\nCFG.MODEL.ARCH = MODEL_ARCH\nCFG.MODEL.PARAM = MODEL_PARAM\nCFG.MODEL.FORWARD_FEATURES = [0, 1, 2]\nCFG.MODEL.TARGET_FEATURES = [0]\n\n# Metrics\nCFG.METRICS = EasyDict()\nCFG.METRICS.FUNCS = EasyDict({\n    \'MAE\': masked_mae,\n    \'MAPE\': masked_mape,\n    \'RMSE\': masked_rmse,\n})\nCFG.METRICS.TARGET = \'MAE\'\nCFG.METRICS.NULL_VAL = NULL_VAL\n\n# Training\nCFG.TRAIN = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.NUM_EPOCHS = NUM_EPOCHS\nCFG.TRAIN.CKPT_SAVE_DIR = os.path.join(\n    \'checkpoints\',\n    MODEL_ARCH.__name__,\n    \'_\'.join([DATA_NAME, str(CFG.TRAIN.NUM_EPOCHS), str(INPUT_LEN), str(OUTPUT_LEN)])\n)\nCFG.TRAIN.LOSS = masked_mae\n\n# Optimizer\nCFG.TRAIN.OPTIM = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.OPTIM.TYPE = "Adam"\nCFG.TRAIN.OPTIM.PARAM = {\n    "lr": 0.002,\n    "weight_decay": 1.0e-5,\n    "eps": 1.0e-8\n}\n\n# Learning Rate Scheduler\nCFG.TRAIN.LR_SCHEDULER = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.LR_SCHEDULER.TYPE = "MultiStepLR"\nCFG.TRAIN.LR_SCHEDULER.PARAM = {\n    "milestones": [1, 30, 38, 46, 54, 62, 70, 80],\n    "gamma": 0.5\n}\n\n# Train Data Loader\nCFG.TRAIN.DATA = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.DATA.BATCH_SIZE = 128\nCFG.TRAIN.DATA.SHUFFLE = True\n\n# Gradient Clipping\nCFG.TRAIN.CLIP_GRAD_PARAM = {\n    "max_norm": 5.0\n}\n\n# Curriculum Learning\nCFG.TRAIN.CL = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.CL.WARM_EPOCHS = 0\nCFG.TRAIN.CL.CL_EPOCHS = 6\nCFG.TRAIN.CL.PREDICTION_LENGTH = 12\n\n# Validation\nCFG.VAL = EasyDict()\nCFG.VAL.INTERVAL = 1\nCFG.VAL.DATA = EasyDict()\nCFG.VAL.DATA.BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n# Test\nCFG.TEST = EasyDict()\nCFG.TEST.INTERVAL = 1\nCFG.TEST.DATA = EasyDict()\nCFG.TEST.DATA.BATCH_SIZE = 64\n\n# Evaluation\nCFG.EVAL = EasyDict()\nCFG.EVAL.HORIZONS = [3, 6, 12]  # 15, 30, 60 minutes\nCFG.EVAL.USE_GPU = True\n```\n\n### 2.2 PEMS-BAY Configuration (PEMS-BAY.py)\n\n```python\n# Same structure as METR-LA but with:\n\nDATA_NAME = \'PEMS-BAY\'  # 325 sensors\nNUM_NODES = 325\n\n# Curriculum Learning for harder dataset\nCFG.TRAIN.CL = EasyDict()\nCFG.TRAIN.CL.WARM_EPOCHS = 30      # More warm-up\nCFG.TRAIN.CL.CL_EPOCHS = 3         # Shorter curriculum phase\nCFG.TRAIN.CL.PREDICTION_LENGTH = 12\n\n# Different batch sizes\nCFG.TRAIN.DATA.BATCH_SIZE = 64      # Smaller batch\nCFG.VAL.DATA.BATCH_SIZE = 128       # Larger validation batch\nCFG.TEST.DATA.BATCH_SIZE = 128      # Larger test batch\n\n# Dataset split\nTRAIN_VAL_TEST_RATIO = [0.7, 0.1, 0.2]  # 70/10/20 split\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Cross-Attention Fusion Mechanism\n\n### 3.1 Multi-Head Attention Formula\n```python\n# Query from spatial-temporal encoder\nQ = E_st @ W_Q\n\n# Key and Value from event text encoder\nK = E_text @ W_K\nV = E_text @ W_V\n\n# Scaled dot-product attention\nhead_i = softmax(Q @ K^T / sqrt(d_k)) @ V\n\n# Concatenate multiple heads\noutput = Concat(head1, ..., headh) @ W_O\n\n# Add residual connection and layer norm\nH_C = LayerNorm(MHA(Q, K, V) + E_st)\n\n# Pass through feed-forward network\nH_fused = LayerNorm(H_C + FFN(H_C))\n```\n\n### 3.2 Key Implementation Details\n```python\n# Embedding dimensions\nembedding_dim = 1024  # Unified dimension for both modalities\n\n# Number of attention heads\nnum_heads = 8\nhead_dim = embedding_dim // num_heads\n\n# Query comes from traffic data\n# Keys and Values come from event embeddings\n# This enables event information to modulate traffic representations\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. LLM Prompt Design Variants\n\n### 4.1 Full Feature Prompt (P1)\n```\nFor each sensor, identify nearby events that could impact traffic \n(e.g., LA news, Severe Weather, concerts, crime). \nExample: Classic Cinema Night at Cinegrill Theater.\n```\n\n### 4.2 Single Event Prompt (P2)\n```\nFor each sensor, identify the most influential event that could impact traffic \n(e.g., LA news, Severe Weather, concerts, crime). \nExample: Classic Cinema Night at Cinegrill Theater.\n```\n\n### 4.3 Without Weather Prompt (P3)\n```\nFor each sensor, identify nearby events that could impact traffic \n(e.g., LA news, concerts, crime). \nExample: Classic Cinema Night at Cinegrill Theater.\n```\n\n### 4.4 Zero-Shot Prompt (P5)\n```\nFor each sensor, identify nearby events that could impact traffic \n(e.g., LA news, Severe Weather, concerts).\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Data Preprocessing Pipeline\n\n### 5.1 Event Data Processing\n```python\n# Step 1: Load sensor coordinates\ncoordinates = read_coordinates_from_file("graph_sensor_locations.txt")\n# Output: List of 207 (or 325/358) coordinate strings\n\n# Step 2: Load temporal data\ntimes = read_time_from_file("METR-LA.h5")\n# Output: Array of timestamps\n\n# Step 3: For each timestamp, generate LLM prompt\nfor timestamp in times:\n    prompt = f"""\n    You are a traffic analysis assistant for Los Angeles (LA).\n    You need to consider events occurring 60 to 115 minutes after \n    each timestamp that could affect traffic flow.\n    \n    ### Date and Time: {timestamp}\n    ### Geographic Coordinates: {coordinates}\n    \n    For each sensor and timestamp, identify nearby event that \n    could impact traffic (e.g., Local news, Severe Weather, \n    concerts, crime).\n    Return a list of {len(coordinates)} items for all sensors.\n    """\n\n# Step 4: Call Gemini 2.5 Pro API\nresponse = client.models.generate_content(\n    model="gemini-2.5-pro-preview-03-25",\n    contents=prompt,\n    config=types.GenerateContentConfig(\n        response_mime_type=\'application/json\',\n        response_schema={...}\n    )\n)\n\n# Step 5: Extract JSON event descriptions\nevents = json.loads(response.text)\n\n# Step 6: Generate text embeddings\nmodel = TextEmbeddingModel.from_pretrained("text-embedding-005")\nembeddings = model.get_embeddings([events_text])\n\n# Step 7: Store as float32 compressed numpy\ntext_emds.append(embeddings[0].values)  # 768-dim vector\n\n# Step 8: Save compressed format\nnp.savez_compressed(\'METR.npz\', embeddings=np.array(text_emds, dtype=np.float32))\n```\n\n### 5.2 Traffic Data Processing\n```python\n# Load from HDF5\ndf = pd.read_hdf(\'METR-LA.h5\')\ntraffic_data = df.values  # N x T tensor (207 x 34272 for METR-LA)\n\n# Z-score normalization (per-channel)\nscaler = ZScoreScaler()\nnormalized_data = scaler.fit_transform(traffic_data)\n\n# Train/Val/Test split (70/10/20)\ntrain_size = int(0.7 * len(traffic_data))\nval_size = int(0.1 * len(traffic_data))\n\ntrain_data = normalized_data[:train_size]\nval_data = normalized_data[train_size:train_size + val_size]\ntest_data = normalized_data[train_size + val_size:]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Key Performance Metrics\n\n### 6.1 Baseline Comparison Table (METR-LA)\n\n| Model | 15 min MAE | 30 min MAE | 60 min MAE | Avg MAE |\n|-------|-----------|-----------|-----------|----------|\n| GraphWaveNet | 2.70 | 3.09 | 3.52 | 3.10 |\n| STWave | 2.83 | 3.22 | 3.55 | 3.20 |\n| D2STGNN | 2.57 | 2.99 | 3.42 | 3.00 |\n| DIGC-Net | 2.88 | 3.18 | 3.49 | 3.19 |\n| STORM | 2.64 | 3.00 | 3.45 | 3.03 |\n| T3 | 2.56 | 2.98 | 3.46 | 3.00 |\n| UrbanGPT | 3.02 | 3.28 | 3.50 | 3.27 |\n| STD-PLM | 2.62 | 3.05 | 3.38 | 3.02 |\n| **FUSE-Traffic** | **2.53** | **2.90** | **3.39** | **2.94** |\n\n### 6.2 Performance Improvement Analysis\n```\nFUSE-Traffic vs D2STGNN (best GNN baseline):\n- 15 min horizon: 2.53 vs 2.57 (-1.6% MAE improvement)\n- 30 min horizon: 2.90 vs 2.99 (-3.0% improvement)\n- 60 min horizon: 3.39 vs 3.42 (-0.9% improvement)\n- Average: 2.94 vs 3.00 (-2.0% improvement)\n\nFUSE-Traffic vs STORM (best fusion baseline):\n- 15 min horizon: 2.53 vs 2.64 (-4.2% MAE improvement)\n- 30 min horizon: 2.90 vs 3.00 (-3.3% improvement)\n- 60 min horizon: 3.39 vs 3.45 (-1.7% improvement)\n- Average: 2.94 vs 3.03 (-3.0% improvement)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Integration Points for LibCity\n\n### 7.1 Model Class Interface\n```python\nclass FUSETraffic(nn.Module):\n    """FUSE-Traffic model class for LibCity integration"""\n    \n    def __init__(self, config):\n        super(FUSETraffic, self).__init__()\n        \n        # Spatial-temporal graph encoder (D2STGNN)\n        self.graph_encoder = D2STGNN(\n            num_nodes=config[\'num_nodes\'],\n            num_feat=config[\'num_feat\'],\n            num_hidden=config[\'num_hidden\'],\n            num_layers=config[\'num_layers\'],\n            dropout=config[\'dropout\'],\n            # ... other D2STGNN parameters\n        )\n        \n        # Text encoder (pretrained, frozen)\n        self.text_encoder = SentenceTransformer(\'model-name\')\n        for param in self.text_encoder.parameters():\n            param.requires_grad = False\n        \n        # Fusion and alignment\n        self.fusion = CrossAttentionFusion(\n            embedding_dim=config[\'embedding_dim\'],\n            num_heads=config[\'num_heads\'],\n        )\n        \n        # Decoder\n        self.decoder = nn.Linear(\n            config[\'embedding_dim\'],\n            config[\'num_nodes\'] * config[\'output_len\']\n        )\n    \n    def forward(self, x_traffic, x_events):\n        # x_traffic: [batch, time, nodes]\n        # x_events: [batch, nodes, event_embedding_dim]\n        \n        # Encode spatial-temporal patterns\n        e_st = self.graph_encoder(x_traffic)  # [batch, nodes, embedding_dim]\n        \n        # Encode event text\n        e_text = self.text_encoder(x_events)  # [batch, nodes, embedding_dim]\n        \n        # Fuse using cross-attention\n        h_fused = self.fusion(e_st, e_text)  # [batch, nodes, embedding_dim]\n        \n        # Decode to predictions\n        y_hat = self.decoder(h_fused)  # [batch, nodes, output_len]\n        \n        return y_hat\n```\n\n### 7.2 Configuration Template\n```python\nMODEL_CONFIG = {\n    \'model_name\': \'FUSE-Traffic\',\n    \'encoder\': {\n        \'base_model\': \'D2STGNN\',\n        \'num_nodes\': 207,\n        \'num_features\': 1,\n        \'hidden_dim\': 32,\n        \'num_layers\': 5,\n        \'dropout\': 0.1,\n        \'temporal_kernel\': 3,\n        \'spatial_kernel\': 2,\n        \'gap\': 3,\n    },\n    \'event_processor\': {\n        \'text_encoder\': \'sentence-transformers/all-mpnet-base-v2\',\n        \'embedding_dim\': 768,\n        \'frozen\': True,\n    },\n    \'fusion\': {\n        \'mechanism\': \'cross-attention\',\n        \'unified_embedding_dim\': 1024,\n        \'num_heads\': 8,\n    },\n    \'training\': {\n        \'epochs\': 100,\n        \'optimizer\': \'Adam\',\n        \'learning_rate\': 0.002,\n        \'weight_decay\': 1e-5,\n        \'scheduler\': \'MultiStepLR\',\n        \'milestones\': [1, 30, 38, 46, 54, 62, 70, 80],\n        \'gamma\': 0.5,\n        \'batch_size\': 128,\n        \'gradient_clip\': 5.0,\n    },\n    \'curriculum_learning\': {\n        \'enabled\': True,\n        \'warm_epochs\': 30,\n        \'cl_epochs\': 3,\n        \'max_prediction_length\': 12,\n    },\n    \'datasets\': {\n        \'METR-LA\': {\'nodes\': 207, \'timesteps\': 34272},\n        \'PEMS-BAY\': {\'nodes\': 325, \'timesteps\': 52116},\n        \'PEMS03\': {\'nodes\': 358, \'timesteps\': 26208},\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n**Document Generated**: January 23, 2026\n**Purpose**: Code reference guide for FUSE-Traffic migration to LibCity\nEOF\ncat /ho