nce=10 epochs\n\nCURRICULUM LEARNING:\n- METR-LA: 0 warm epochs + 6 CL epochs\n- PEMS-BAY: 30 warm epochs + 3 CL epochs\n- PEMS03: Standard curriculum applied\n- Purpose: Gradually increase prediction length complexity\n\nFUSION MECHANISM:\n- Type: Cross-Attention with multi-head attention\n- Query source: Spatial-temporal traffic embeddings (E_st)\n- Key/Value source: Event text embeddings (E_text)\n- Transformation: Attention output + residual connection\n- Layer norm + Feed-forward + Layer norm\n- Result: Fused embeddings (H_fused) for decoder\n\n================================================================================\n7. PERFORMANCE RESULTS\n================================================================================\n\nMETR-LA DATASET (207 sensors, 34,272 timesteps):\nRanking by Average MAE:\n1. FUSE-Traffic: 2.94 (15min: 2.53, 30min: 2.90, 60min: 3.39)\n2. T3: 3.00 (15min: 2.56, 30min: 2.98, 60min: 3.46)\n3. D2STGNN: 3.00 (15min: 2.57, 30min: 2.99, 60min: 3.42)\n4. STORM: 3.03 (15min: 2.64, 30min: 3.00, 60min: 3.45)\n5. GraphWaveNet: 3.10 (15min: 2.70, 30min: 3.09, 60min: 3.52)\n\nPEMS-BAY DATASET (325 sensors, 52,116 timesteps):\n1. FUSE-Traffic: 1.58\n2. T3: 1.63\n3. D2STGNN: 1.68\n4. GraphWaveNet: 1.66\n5. STWave: 1.64\n\nPEMS03 DATASET (358 sensors, 26,208 timesteps):\n1. FUSE-Traffic: 15.05\n2. STD-PLM: 16.47\n3. STORM: 17.03\n4. UrbanGPT: 18.17\n5. GraphWaveNet: 15.81\n\nIMPROVEMENT ANALYSIS:\n- vs D2STGNN (best GNN): 2.0% average improvement\n- vs STORM (best fusion): 3.0% average improvement\n- Special strength: High-impact event scenarios (4.2-15% improvement)\n\nEVENT IMPACT DISTRIBUTION:\n- No impact: ~60% of timestamps\n- Minor impact: ~10-15%\n- Moderate impact: ~15%\n- High impact: ~5-10%\n\nABLATION STUDIES:\n1. Prompt design: Full features > weather-only > crime-only > zero-shot\n2. Fusion mechanism: Cross-attention > gating > addition > concatenation\n3. Optimal hyperparameters: 2 MLP layers, 512 embedding dimension\n\n============